  "reading": "ぬかる",
  "romaji": "nukaru",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (godan)",
  "gloss": "to become muddy; to be miry",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to become muddy; to be miry",
      "explanation": "Of ground or a road, to turn soft and muddy so that feet sink in, typically after rain or snowmelt."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "27927_nukaru_ex1",
      "japanese": "⟦{道|みち}→道：00505_michi⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧ぬかって⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧。",
      "english": "The road is muddy.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "27927_nukaru_ex2",
      "japanese": "⟦{雨|あめ}→雨：00583_ame⟧⟦で→で：00502_de⟧⟦{庭|にわ}→庭：02239_niwa⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧ぬかってしまった。",
      "english": "The garden has gotten muddy from the rain.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "27927_nukaru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{雪|ゆき}どけ⟦で→で：00502_de⟧⟦{足元|あしもと}→足元：04096_ashimoto⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧ぬかって⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧⟦の→の：09472_no⟧で{気|き}をつけて。",
      "english": "The ground underfoot is muddy from the melting snow, so be careful.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Used of ground or roads turning soft and muddy after rain or melting snow. Despite ending in る, it is a godan verb (ぬ⟦から→から：00504_kara⟧・⟦ない→ない：01118_nai⟧, ぬかっ・て).\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Intransitive. The subject is the ground that becomes muddy: ⟦{道|みち}→道：00505_michi⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧ぬかる.\n\nASPECT (ている):\n- ぬかって⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧ describes the resulting muddy state ('is muddy'), not an action in progress.\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- ぬかるみ: a muddy spot; mire — the noun form, naming the muddy ground itself",
